><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20251008123027+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="2b611e98-0767-4029-a513-bfb2f98862d1" date="D:20251008123027+10'00'" name="e3fe8db6-5cf6-46ba-aced-975c30cdd4a0" icon="Comment" page="10" rect="318.419189,476.343353,342.419189,500.343353" subject="Sticky Note" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>The influence of cadence&#xD;on the yaw behaviour within the frame triangle appears to be minimal,&#xD;but the mannequin-based tests indicate a strong effect of reduced frequency&#xD;on both the pitch and speed variations which have not been&#xD;identified in previous research.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
